Z||000001||Boomtastic||07-08-2001||09:05 AM||||I'm cheating. In Mass., vehicles must go on the dyno to be tested. My car cannot go on the dyno because the wheelie bars are in the way. Place your bets that they will NOT be removed prior to to the testing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> In a case where the vehicle cannot fit on the dyno (other cars have this problem, especially lowered vehicles with ground effects) the inspector does what is called a "2 step idle test" where they rev the motor and test it under 2 different RPMs. Hopefully that (and small token of my appreciation in the form of a monetary gift) will get me passed through ..||||reg||1
